From: Arkadiusz Miśkiewicz <arekm@maven.pl>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:41:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mysqlnd: stop mnd_pestrndup() at the length before reading a byte

_mysqlnd_pestrndup() tested *p before the remaining length, so a string
not NUL-terminated within length (every length-prefixed server string:
OK packet and auth response messages) had the byte after it read. For a
message that ends the packet that byte is outside the packet (and past
the command buffer when the packet fills it); valgrind reports it as an
uninitialised read on the new OK packet message test. Check the length
first.
PLD: taken from packages/php branch PHP_7_1, php-mysqlnd-pestrndup.patch
---
 ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_alloc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_alloc.c b/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_alloc.c
index aa4c598a..56acabf9 100644
--- a/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_alloc.c
+++ b/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_alloc.c
@@ -562,7 +562,7 @@ char * _mysqlnd_pestrndup(const char * const ptr, size_t length, zend_bool persi
 		size_t l = length;
 		char * p = (char *) ptr;
 		char * dest = (char *) FAKE_PTR(ret);
-		while (*p && l--) {
+		while (l-- && *p) {
 			*dest++ = *p++;
 		}
 		*dest = '\0';
